  "final_span": ".\n\"It's going great, fantastic,\" Fischer said of the summer. \"It's an amazing experience coming in my rookie year and playing with so many great, experienced girls.\n\"I think that's what's so fantastic about water polo is that everyone goes way back and everyone's always so supportive and everyone's just so much fun to play with and it's so unrealistic that in a game situation you're basically playing on your own for the whole match.\"\nThe U.S. maintained a tough stance and scored points offensively and in terms of goals, putting itself in a game against Russia, as Fischer noted.\n\"We just really got to work the ball and getting good looks and taking advantage of those chances we had,\" she said. \"We really just have to continue to get good shots off and not stop and not be afraid of the pace, pace it up, and beat the goalie.\"\nThe U.S. possesses three top-tier attackers with positions similar to No. 3, including Fischer, Neushul, and Grossman. They've got Hall of Famer Alys Williams, too.\n\"It's it's definitely great to have three No. 3s and definitely with the way Alys is playing it's always great to be behind Aly,\" Fischer said.\nOver the long pool playing schedule in a short period of time, \"you're going to have ups and you're going to have downs,\" Fischer said.\n\"You just can't have a losing mentality and can't get caught up in your last game because this game is so important. So you just have to make sure you play every single day with good, positive energy and play with a lot of fight to keep winning and to keep climbing and keep improving.\"\nFrom the Dad 2.0 Conference: Registration is now open for the Speak Straight Fathers Online Seminar. Parents will learn how to avoid the mistakes they see others making, and how to appreciate and understand their children in ways they never thought possible. https://speakstraight.com/parents\nLabels: Gabby Stone, KK Clark, Maddie Musselman, Makense Fischer, Rio Olympics, Sacred Heart Prep water polo,",
  "break_point": null
 },
